      page: "/help/glow-e27"
    message: "Good afternoon. I have had Lumen Glow E27 bulbs for about a year and I have a long history with your app, so bear with me. Last winter the app kept logging me out every few days, then after an update in March the scenes I had built disappeared and I had to set them up again. In May I changed my internet provider and had to add every bulb to the app again, which took an evening, although your guide about removing them from the device list and pairing them once more did help. My new router has separate 2.4 GHz and 5 GHz networks and the bulbs are all on the 2.4 GHz one, as the guide says. Everything was fine through the summer. Now the actual problem: the bulb in the hallway has started to flicker quickly and constantly, even at full brightness and even when the app is closed and the phone is off. I reset it with the five on-off switches, it blinked three times and paired again, and ten minutes later it was flickering again. The other five bulbs on the same network are fine. I also swapped it with the one from the bedroom, and the flicker moved with the bulb, so it is the bulb and not the socket. I would like to know what you can do about this bulb. And, separately, will the app ever keep my scenes after an update?"
    order_id: "LUM-20250918"
    product:
      sku: "SKU-GL27E1"
      name: "Lumen Glow E27"
